  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Science for a Water Secure Latin America and the Caribbean in a Changing Environment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This element will support Member States in the implementation of IHP-IX in LAC, based on its Strategic and Operational Implementation Plans, with a focus on accelerating change towards the targets of SDG6. It will work closely with IHP working groups, UNESCO Chairs and UNESCO Centres in the region to address priority areas in (1) scientific research and innovation, (2) water education in Fourth Industrial Revolution including sustainability, (3) bridging the data-knowledge gap, (4) integrated water resources management under conditions of global change, and (5) water governance based on science for mitigation, adaptation, and resilience. It will also support regional working groups working on cryosphere and forest systems, while promoting intersectoral and interagency cooperation.</narrative>
  </description>
